{
  "raw": {
    "https://careers.twc.edu.hk/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Research-Track%29-in-Psychology-and-Social-Sciences-1055/1361659166/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Research Track) in Psychology and Social Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Research Track) in Psychology and Social Sciences Job Details | TWC Skip to main content Search by Keyword Language English (United Kingdom) View profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Category All Unit / School All Apply now » Assistant Professor (Research Track) in Psychology and Social Sciences Tung Wah College Established by Tung Wah Group of Hospitals (“TWGHs”) in 2010, Tung Wah College (TWC) is a self-financing degree-granting institution registered under the Post Secondary Colleges Ordinance (Cap.320).  Following the educational ideals of TWGHs and leveraging on its renowned strengths and expertise, TWC aims to provide high quality tertiary education to nurture competent, socially responsible and caring professionals for the benefits of society. With the staunch support of TWGHs, TWC has been developing rapidly and built up a niche in healthcare education. It is the first self-financing tertiary institution offering six professionally accredited degrees to train nurses and allied health professionals such as medical laboratory technologists, occupational therapists, diagnostic radiographer, therapeutic radiographer and physiotherapists. Besides, the College is also the first institution registered under Cap. 320 offering early childhood education degree and higher diploma programmes to train qualified kindergarten teachers and childcare professionals. Currently, TWC has 4 schools (namely School of Arts and Humanities, School of Management, School of Medical and Health Sciences, and School of Nursing) running a total of 20 doctoral degree, bachelor degree, sub-degree, diploma and certificate programmes in various disciplines.  It has a student population of around 5,000 in 2025/2026 and nurtured more than 7,200 graduates since its inception in 2010. Being a young and vibrant institution, TWC aspires to become a leading private university in the long term.  It is planning to launch a number of new programmes, strengthen teaching and learning facilities and quality, and enhance research capability etc. in coming years.  To cope with its continuous development, we are now inviting highly qualified candidates to fill the following post: Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be required but not limited to: support all aspects of academic activities through teaching, research, and consultancy; contribute to the planning, formulation and implementation of the College and School’s strategic initiatives and development; participate in programme development and validation exercises; take up responsibilities in academic and departmental administration; guide / facilitate the College in enhancing its visibility and strengthening its local and international connections; take the initiative in promoting good teaching and collaborative research; supervise and support the work of lecturers involved in prescribed courses/programmes; teach courses / subjects according to the operational needs of the College; liaise with external bodies for job placements and professional development; engage in research and have deliverables (grants and publications), in accordance with the workload requirements of the College; perform scholarly activities; increase the research output and raise the level of consultancies in respective discipline(s); oversee / perform academic activities including academic advising, examination and assessment, student recruitment, committee works, whole person development activities of students; undertake professional service to external professional body / organization and provide public services to the community; and perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications and Experience Required The appointee should have: a PhD degree or equivalent professional Doctorate in a relevant discipline; some relevant experience in teaching, research or professional service; ability to liaise and effectively communicate with relevant sections of the community, professional bodies, government departments and other external organizations; and track record in obtaining competitive research funding and publications in international peer review journals; Application Salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. To apply, please submit your application via system.  The College reserves the right to fill or not to fill the post.  Applicants who are not contacted by the College 6 months after the application deadline may consider their applications unsuccessful. For enquiries, please phone or send WhatsApp to 9172-8618. Application Deadline: Until the position is filled All information and personal data collected will be used solely for recruitment related purposes. For more information about the College, please visit our website: https://www.twc.edu.hk . WE ARE AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITIES EMPLOYER Apply now » Find similar jobs: Corporate Website Copyright & Disclaimer Privacy Policy ©2025 Tung Wah College Limited. All Rights Reserved"
    },
    "https://careers.twc.edu.hk/job/Associate-Professor-%28Research-Track%29-Assistant-Professor-%28Research-Track%29-626/1328284066/": {
      "title": "Associate Professor (Research Track) / Assistant Professor (Research Track)",
      "description": "Associate Professor (Research Track) / Assistant Professor (Research Track) Job Details | TWC Skip to main content Search by Keyword Language English (United Kingdom) View profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Category All Unit / School All Apply now » Associate Professor (Research Track) / Assistant Professor (Research Track) Tung Wah College Established by Tung Wah Group of Hospitals (“TWGHs”) in 2010, Tung Wah College (TWC) is a self-financing degree-granting institution registered under the Post Secondary Colleges Ordinance (Cap.320). Following the educational ideals of TWGHs and leveraging on its renowned strengths and expertise, TWC aims to provide high quality tertiary education to nurture competent, socially responsible and caring professionals for the benefits of society. With the staunch support of TWGHs, TWC has been developing rapidly and built up a niche in healthcare education. It is the first self-financing tertiary institution offering six professionally accredited degrees to train nurses and allied health professionals such as medical laboratory technologists, occupational therapists, diagnostic radiographer, therapeutic radiographer and physiotherapists. Besides, the College is also the first institution registered under Cap. 320 offering early childhood education degree and higher diploma programmes to train qualified kindergarten teachers and childcare professionals. Currently, TWC has 4 schools (namely School of Arts and Humanities, School of Management, School of Medical and Health Sciences, and School of Nursing) running a total of 20 doctoral degree, bachelor degree, sub-degree, diploma and certificate programmes in various disciplines.  It has a student population of around 5,000 in 2025/2026 and nurtured more than 7,200 graduates since its inception in 2010. Being a young and vibrant institution, TWC aspires to become a leading private university in the long term.  It is planning to launch a number of new programmes, strengthen teaching and learning facilities and quality, and enhance research capability etc. in coming years.  To cope with its continuous development, we are now inviting highly qualified candidates to fill the following post: Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be required but not limited to: support all aspects of academic activities through teaching, research, and consultancy; contribute to the planning, formulation and implementation of the College and School’s strategic initiatives and development; participate in programme development and validation exercises; take up responsibilities in academic and departmental administration and clinical teaching; guide / facilitate the College in enhancing its visibility and strengthening its local and international connections; take the initiative in promoting good teaching and collaborative research; liaise with external bodies for job placements and professional development; engage in research and have publication output, in accordance to the workload requirements of the College; perform scholarly activities; increase the publication output and raise the level of consultancies in respective discipline(s); oversee / perform academic activities including academic advising, examination and assessment, student recruitment, committee works, whole person development activities of students; undertake professional service to external professional body / organization and provide public services to the community; and perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications and Experience Required The appointee should have: a PhD degree or equivalent professional Doctorate in a relevant discipline (obstetric nursing background is preferred) with a valid Registered Nurse practicing certificate (General and/or Mental Health) issued by the Nursing Council of Hong Kong; sufficient years of relevant experience in teaching in the tertiary education sector, programme development and programme leadership;and publications in journals (desirably with international reputation) and with high impact in the relevant discipline; and demonstration as an active researcher. Application Salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. To apply, please submit your application via system.  The College reserves the right to fill or not to fill the post.  Applicants who are not contacted by the College 6 months after the application deadline may consider their applications unsuccessful. For enquiries, please phone or send WhatsApp to 9172-8618. Application Deadline: Until the position(s) is/are filled All information and personal data collected will be used solely for recruitment related purposes. For more information about the College, please visit our website: https://www.twc.edu.hk . Tung Wah College is an equal opportunities employer. We embrace the values of equality, diversity and inclusion and are dedicated to fostering an environment that respects and supports people with diverse perspectives, abilities, cultures and experiences. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Corporate Website Copyright & Disclaimer Privacy Policy ©2025 Tung Wah College Limited. All Rights Reserved"
    },
    "https://careers.twc.edu.hk/job/Associate-ProfessorAssistant-Professor%28Research-Track%29-in-Occupational-Therapy-668/1328873166/": {
      "title": "Associate Professor/Assistant Professor(Research Track) in Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Associate Professor/Assistant Professor(Research Track) in Occupational Therapy Job Details | TWC Skip to main content Search by Keyword Language English (United Kingdom) View profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Category All Unit / School All Apply now » Associate Professor/Assistant Professor(Research Track) in Occupational Therapy Tung Wah College Established by Tung Wah Group of Hospitals (“TWGHs”) in 2010, Tung Wah College (TWC) is a self-financing degree-granting institution registered under the Post Secondary Colleges Ordinance (Cap.320).  Following the educational ideals of TWGHs and leveraging on its renowned strengths and expertise, TWC aims to provide high quality tertiary education to nurture competent, socially responsible and caring professionals for the benefits of society. With the staunch support of TWGHs, TWC has been developing rapidly and built up a niche in healthcare education. It is the first self-financing tertiary institution offering five professionally accredited degrees to train nurses and allied health professionals such as medical laboratory technologists, occupational therapists, radiation therapists and physiotherapists. Besides, the College is also the first institution registered under Cap. 320 offering early childhood education degree and higher diploma programmes to train qualified kindergarten teachers and childcare professionals. Currently, TWC has 4 schools (namely School of Arts and Humanities, School of Management, School of Medical and Health Sciences, and School of Nursing) running a total of 19 degree, sub-degree, diploma and certificate programmes in several disciplines.  It has a student population of around 5,000 in 2025/2026 and nurtured more than 7,200 graduates since its inception in 2010. Being a young and vibrant institution, TWC aspires to become a leading private university in the long term.  It is planning to launch a number of new programmes, strengthen teaching and learning facilities and quality, and enhance research capability etc. in coming years.  To cope with its continuous development, we are now inviting highly qualified candidates to fill the following post: Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will: 1.    support all aspects of academic activities through teaching, research, and consultancy; 2.    contribute to the planning, formulation and implementation of the College and School’s strategic initiatives and development; 3.    facilitate / participate in programme development and validation exercises; 4.    take up responsibilities in academic and departmental administration and clinical teaching; 5.    guide / facilitate the College in enhancing its visibility and strengthening its local and international connections; 6.    take the initiative in promoting good teaching and collaborative research; 7.    liaise with external bodies for job placements and professional development; 8.    engage in research including seeking external grants and has publication output in accordance with the workload requirements of the College; 9.    perform scholarly activities; increase the publication output and raise the level of consultancies in respective discipline(s); 10.  oversee / perform other academic activities including academic advising, examination and assessment, student recruitment, committee works, whole person development activities of students; 11.  undertake professional service to external professional body / organization and provide public services to the community; and 12.  perform any other duties as assigned. Qualifications and Experience Required Applicants should: 1.    possess a PhD degree / Professional Doctorate in a relevant discipline with sufficient years of relevant experience in teaching in the tertiary education sector, programme development and / or programme leadership; 2.    possess a valid practicing certificate issued by the relevant professional body; 3.    have publications in journals (desirably with international reputation) and with high impact in the relevant discipline; and 4.    possess a good track record as an active researcher. Application Salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. To apply, please submit your application via system.  The College reserves the right to fill or not to fill the post.  Applicants who are not contacted by the College 6 months after the application deadline may consider their applications unsuccessful. For enquiries, please phone or send WhatsApp to 9172-8618. Application Deadline: Until the position(s) is/are filled All information and personal data collected will be used solely for recruitment related purposes. For more information about the College, please visit our website: https://www.twc.edu.hk . WE ARE AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITIES EMPLOYER Apply now » Find similar jobs: Corporate Website Copyright & Disclaimer Privacy Policy ©2025 Tung Wah College Limited. All Rights Reserved"
    },
    "https://careers.twc.edu.hk/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Research-Track%29-1324/1367795066/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Research Track)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Research Track) Job Details | TWC Skip to main content Search by Keyword Language English (United Kingdom) View profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Category All Unit / School All Apply now » Assistant Professor (Research Track) Tung Wah College Established by Tung Wah Group of Hospitals (“TWGHs”) in 2010, Tung Wah College (TWC) is a self-financing degree-granting institution registered under the Post Secondary Colleges Ordinance (Cap.320). Following the educational ideals of TWGHs and leveraging on its renowned strengths and expertise, TWC aims to provide high quality tertiary education to nurture competent, socially responsible and caring professionals for the benefits of society. With the staunch support of TWGHs, TWC has been developing rapidly and built up a niche in healthcare education. It is the first self-financing tertiary institution offering six professionally accredited degrees to train nurses and allied health professionals such as medical laboratory technologists, occupational therapists, diagnostic radiographer, therapeutic radiographer and physiotherapists. Besides, the College is also the first institution registered under Cap. 320 offering early childhood education degree and higher diploma programmes to train qualified kindergarten teachers and childcare professionals. Currently, TWC has 4 schools (namely School of Arts and Humanities, School of Management, School of Medical and Health Sciences, and School of Nursing) running a total of 20 doctoral degree, bachelor degree, sub-degree, diploma and certificate programmes in various disciplines.  It has a student population of around 5,000 in 2025/2026 and nurtured more than 7,200 graduates since its inception in 2010. Being a young and vibrant institution, TWC aspires to become a leading private university in the long term.  It is planning to launch a number of new programmes, strengthen teaching and learning facilities and quality, and enhance research capability etc. in coming years.  To cope with its continuous development, we are now inviting highly qualified candidates to fill the following post: About the Position We invite applications for an Assistant Professor (Research Track) position to support our School’s research efforts and academic programmes in the following areas: Management and application of artificial intelligence in organisations; Low-altitude economy applications in organisations; Organisational innovation. This role encompasses both engagement in research activities, as well as teaching and curriculum development and enhancement. Applicants are expected to engage in both undergraduate and postgraduate teaching in English and Putonghua. Duties and Responsibilities 1. Engagement in Research Activities: Publish articles in academic journals; Obtain competitive grants and/or industry grants for research; Collaborate with colleagues on research projects; Publish cases and teaching notes. 2. Teaching and Curriculum Development and Enhancement: Develop and review programme curricula and contribute to programme accreditation exercises; Deliver high-quality instruction at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels; Develop and enhance course materials and assessments aligned with programme objectives; Supervise students' research projects and provide mentorship throughout their academic journeys. 3. Professional Development: Stay updated on trends and advancements in management, integrating relevant content into teaching; Engage in professional development opportunities to enhance research and teaching effectiveness and subject matter expertise. ​​​​​​​4. Collaboration and Engagement: Foster collaborative relationships with faculty from other disciplines to enhance interprofessional research and education; Contribute to initiatives that promote interdisciplinary learning among students. ​​​​​​​5. Service: Engage in activities that promote the School’s academic programmes within the College and the broader community. Qualifications and Experience Required PhD or equivalent Doctoral qualification in a relevant field; Demonstrated expertise in various management-related disciplines; Effective communication and interpersonal skills; Teaching experience at the higher education level; Proficiency in spoken and written English and Putonghua. Application Salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. To apply, please submit your application via system.  The College reserves the right to fill or not to fill the post.  Applicants who are not contacted by the College 6 months after the application deadline may consider their applications unsuccessful. For enquiries, please phone or send WhatsApp to 9172-8618. Application Deadline: Until the position is filled All information and personal data collected will be used solely for recruitment related purposes. For more information about the College, please visit our website: https://www.twc.edu.hk . Tung Wah College is an equal opportunities employer. We embrace the values of equality, diversity and inclusion and are dedicated to fostering an environment that respects and supports people with diverse perspectives, abilities, cultures and experiences. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Corporate Website Copyright & Disclaimer Privacy Policy ©2025 Tung Wah College Limited. All Rights Reserved"
    },
    "https://careers.twc.edu.hk/job/Professor-%28Research-Track%29-635/1328338266/": {
      "title": "Professor (Research Track)",
      "description": "Professor (Research Track) Job Details | TWC Skip to main content Search by Keyword Language English (United Kingdom) View profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Category All Unit / School All Apply now » Professor (Research Track) Tung Wah College Established by Tung Wah Group of Hospitals (“TWGHs”) in 2010, Tung Wah College (TWC) is a self-financing degree-granting institution registered under the Post Secondary Colleges Ordinance (Cap.320).  Following the educational ideals of TWGHs and leveraging on its renowned strengths and expertise, TWC aims to provide high quality tertiary education to nurture competent, socially responsible and caring professionals for the benefits of society. With the staunch support of TWGHs, TWC has been developing rapidly and built up a niche in healthcare education. It is the first self-financing tertiary institution offering five professionally accredited degrees to train nurses and allied health professionals such as medical laboratory technologists, occupational therapists, radiation therapists and physiotherapists. Besides, the College is also the first institution registered under Cap. 320 offering early childhood education degree and higher diploma programmes to train qualified kindergarten teachers and childcare professionals. Currently, TWC has 4 schools (namely School of Arts and Humanities, School of Management, School of Medical and Health Sciences, and School of Nursing) running a total of 19 degree, sub-degree, diploma and certificate programmes in several disciplines.  It has a student population of around 5,000 in 2025/2026 and nurtured more than 7,200 graduates since its inception in 2010. Being a young and vibrant institution, TWC aspires to become a leading private university in the long term.  It is planning to launch a number of new programmes, strengthen teaching and learning facilities and quality, and enhance research capability etc. in coming years.  To cope with its continuous development, we are now inviting highly qualified candidates to fill the following post. Tung Wah College is conducting a global search for a Professor (Research Track) in the School of Medical and Health Sciences to provide academic leadership and foster research excellence. We are seeking a dynamic and innovative candidate with a distinguished record in medical and health sciences, particularly those who leverage modern methodologies to advance the field. Duties and Responsibilities The ideal candidate will have a strong background in applying knowledge to advance education, professional practice, and innovative healthcare development. We welcome applicants with expertise in areas such as allied health, biomedical science, forensic Science, medical laboratory science, public health, neuroscience, or sports science. We are also especially interested in candidates who have strengths in Artificial Intelligence (AI), health data analytics, bioinformatics, or digital health for translational, multidisciplinary research. A proven ability to lead curriculum development, secure competitive grants for applied research, and foster strong community and clinical partnerships is highly desirable. Candidates should be highly self-motivated, be an excellent team player, and eager to contribute to a collaborative, practice-oriented academic setting. The successful candidate is expected to: Develop and lead high-impact applied and translational research projects that address real-world healthcare challenges; Secure and manage significant external research funding; Publish regularly in internationally recognized, high-impact journals while disseminating findings to the wider academic and professional community; Provide academic leadership in teaching, programme development, and professional accreditation; Mentor and supervise postgraduate research students and early-career researchers, fostering a dynamic, inclusive research culture; Actively build and maintain partnerships with local and international healthcare institutions, industry, and the community; Contribute to strategic planning and continuous improvement of the School and College’s research agenda; Engage actively in professional organizations, representing the School in relevant academic, clinical, and community networks; and Perform any other duties as assigned. Qualifications and Experience Required A doctoral degree in a relevant discipline (e.g., Biomedical Science, Forensic, Medical Laboratory Science, Physiotherapy, Public Health, Sports Science, AI, Health Informatics, or a related field), preferably a PhD. Demonstrated substantial experience in leadership roles within the tertiary education sector or in professional organizations. A distinguished record of scholarly achievement commensurate with the rank of Professor. Extensive experience in tertiary education, including curriculum design, teaching, and programme management. A strong track record in applied, practice-based research and competitive grant acquisition. Documented experience in successful supervision of postgraduate students. Registration or eligibility for registration with the relevant professional body in Hong Kong (where applicable) is an advantage Application Salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. To apply, please submit your application via system.  The College reserves the right to fill or not to fill the post.  Applicants who are not contacted by the College 6 months after the application deadline may consider their applications unsuccessful. For enquiries, please phone or send WhatsApp to 9172-8618. Application Deadline: Until the position is filled All information and personal data collected will be used solely for recruitment related purposes. For more information about the College, please visit our website: https://www.twc.edu.hk . WE ARE AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITIES EMPLOYER Apply now » Find similar jobs: Corporate Website Copyright & Disclaimer Privacy Policy ©2025 Tung Wah College Limited. All Rights Reserved"
    },
    "https://careers.twc.edu.hk/job/Professor-Associate-Professor-%28Research-Track%29-in-Division-of-Science-773/1330947666/": {
      "title": "Professor / Associate Professor (Research Track) in Division of Science",
      "description": "Professor / Associate Professor (Research Track) in Division of Science Job Details | TWC Skip to main content Search by Keyword Language English (United Kingdom) View profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Category All Unit / School All Apply now » Professor / Associate Professor (Research Track) in Division of Science Tung Wah College Established by Tung Wah Group of Hospitals (“TWGHs”) in 2010, Tung Wah College (TWC) is a self-financing degree-granting institution registered under the Post Secondary Colleges Ordinance (Cap.320).  Following the educational ideals of TWGHs and leveraging on its renowned strengths and expertise, TWC aims to provide high quality tertiary education to nurture competent, socially responsible and caring professionals for the benefits of society. With the staunch support of TWGHs, TWC has been developing rapidly and built up a niche in healthcare education. It is the first self-financing tertiary institution offering five professionally accredited degrees to train nurses and allied health professionals such as medical laboratory technologists, occupational therapists and radiation therapists. Besides, the College is also the first institution registered under Cap. 320 offering early childhood education degree and higher diploma programmes to train qualified kindergarten teachers and childcare professionals. Currently, TWC has 4 schools (namely School of Arts and Humanities, School of Management, School of Medical and Health Sciences, and School of Nursing) running a total of 19 degree, sub-degree and diploma programmes in several disciplines.  It has a student population of over 4,000 in 2024/2025. Being a young and vibrant institution, TWC aspires to become a leading private university in the long term.  It is planning to launch a number of new programmes, strengthen teaching and learning facilities and quality, and enhance research capability etc. in coming years.  To cope with its continuous development, we are now inviting highly qualified candidates to fill the following post: Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will support all aspects of academic activities including teaching of Biomedical (Molecular Diagnostics, Genetics, Immunology, Biochemistry) and/or Forensic Science courses (e.g. Chemistry. Toxicology, Forensic DNA, Biomedical Criminalistics, Techniques in Human identification and Crime Scene Investigations, and related courses), research, and consultancy; actively contribute to the planning, formulation and implementation of the College and School’s strategic direction and development; take a leading role and participate in programme development and validation exercises; contribute to academic and school administration; lead and supervise the work of academic staff involved in prescribed courses / programmes; take up responsibilities in academic and departmental administration and clinical teaching; guide / facilitate the College in enhancing its visibility and strengthening its local and international connections; build and develop an extensive network of contacts and colleagues to develop and enhance College market position and reputation; provide leadership in promoting good teaching and collaborative research; liaise with external bodies for job placements and professional development; perform scholarly activities; facilitate the development and enhancement of the discipline through quality research and publications including seeking external grants and raise the level of consultancies in respective discipline(s); oversee and perform academic activities including academic advising, examination and assessment, student recruitment, committee works, whole person development activities of students; undertake professional service to external professional body / organization and provide public services to the community. Qualifications and Experience Required For Professor / Associate Professor position, applicants should possess a PhD degree / Professional Doctorate in a relevant discipline with extensive relevant experience in teaching in the tertiary education sector, programme development and programme leadership; publications in journals (desirably with international reputation) and with high impact in the relevant discipline; and demonstration as an active researcher. Application Salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. To apply, please submit your application via system.  The College reserves the right to fill or not to fill the post.  Applicants who are not contacted by the College 6 months after the application deadline may consider their applications unsuccessful. For enquiries, please phone or send WhatsApp to 9172-8618. Application Deadline: Until the position(s) is/are filled All information and personal data collected will be used solely for recruitment related purposes. For more information about the College, please visit our website: https://www.twc.edu.hk . WE ARE AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITIES EMPLOYER Apply now » Find similar jobs: Corporate Website Copyright & Disclaimer Privacy Policy ©2025 Tung Wah College Limited. All Rights Reserved"
    },
    "https://careers.twc.edu.hk/job/Vice-President-%28Research-and-Innovation%29-1065/1361705366/": {
      "title": "Vice President (Research and Innovation) Job Details",
      "description": "Vice President (Research and Innovation) Job Details | TWC Skip to main content Search by Keyword Language English (United Kingdom) View profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Category All Unit / School All Apply now » Vice President (Research and Innovation) Tung Wah College Established by Tung Wah Group of Hospitals (“TWGHs”) in 2010, Tung Wah College (TWC) is a self-financing degree-granting institution registered under the Post Secondary Colleges Ordinance (Cap.320).  Following the educational ideals of TWGHs and leveraging on its renowned strengths and expertise, TWC aims to provide high quality tertiary education to nurture competent, socially responsible and caring professionals for the benefits of society. With the staunch support of TWGHs, TWC has been developing rapidly and built up a niche in healthcare education. It is the first self-financing tertiary institution offering five professionally accredited degrees to train nurses and allied health professionals such as medical laboratory technologists, occupational therapists radiation therapists and physiotherapists. Besides, the College is also the first institution registered under Cap. 320 offering early childhood education degree and higher diploma programmes to train qualified kindergarten teachers and childcare professionals. Currently, TWC has 4 schools (namely School of Arts and Humanities, School of Management, School of Medical and Health Sciences, and School of Nursing) running a total of 19 degree, sub-degree, diploma and certificate programmes in several disciplines.  It has a student population of around 5,000 in 2025/2026 and nurtured more than 7,200 graduates since its inception in 2010. Being a young and vibrant institution, TWC aspires to become a leading private university in the long term.  It is planning to launch a number of new programmes, strengthen teaching and learning facilities and quality, and enhance research capability etc. in coming years.  To cope with its continuous development, we are now inviting highly qualified candidates to fill the following post: Duties and Responsibilities Provide strategic leadership in developing and implementing TWC’s research and innovation agenda, ensuring alignment with institutional priorities, emerging trends, and societal needs. Foster a culture of research excellence, interdisciplinary collaboration, and innovation across faculties and administrative units, enhancing the College’s overall research profile and impact. Collaborate closely with the President and senior leadership to advance institutional priorities, including advising on research, innovation, and knowledge transfer strategies. Oversee the establishment and management of research centres, innovation hubs, and technology transfer initiatives, with emphasis on applied, industry-driven outcomes. Strengthen research capacity by supporting faculty and staff in securing external funding, developing research competencies, and ensuring robust research administration, compliance, and reporting frameworks. Promote knowledge transfer, commercialization, and entrepreneurship, including the development of intellectual property, startups, and industry partnerships. Build and sustain strategic partnerships with industry, government, academia, and community stakeholders locally and internationally, enhancing the College’s visibility and influence. Oversee governance, policies, and compliance in research and innovation, ensuring adherence to ethical standards, regulatory requirements, and effective risk management. Manage research and innovation resources, including budgets, infrastructure, and talent development, to support sustainable growth and institutional ambitions. Advocate for TWC’s research achievements through effective communications and engagement with funding bodies and stakeholders. Qualifications and Experience Required Doctoral degree in a relevant discipline, with academic standing at full professorial level or equivalent experience. Substantial experience in research leadership and academic administration within the tertiary education sector, with a demonstrated ability to build and enhance institutional research capacity and culture. Proven track record in developing and leading research and innovation initiatives, including securing external funding, managing complex programmes, and delivering impactful outcomes. Strong leadership and interpersonal skills, with the ability to foster collaboration across disciplines and build effective partnerships with academic, industry, and community stakeholders. Demonstrated understanding of the higher education landscape and relevant industry environment, with the ability to align research and innovation strategies to institutional and societal priorities. Recognised research profile with evidence of academic and/or professional achievement in the relevant field. Strategic, innovative, and collaborative leadership style, with high integrity and strong commitment to research excellence and institutional development. Excellent communication skills, with proficiency in English and Chinese (Cantonese and Putonghua preferred). Application A fixed-term contract will be offered, with the possibility of renewal subject to performance.  Salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Any interested party may apply by letter setting out in detail why the applicant considers himself or herself suitable for the position, together with a full curriculum vitae, to be sent to Mr. TT Ho of Korn Ferry International (HK) Ltd, 15/F, St George’s Building, 2 Ice House Street, Central, Hong Kong or by email to TWC-VP@kornferry.com.  Review of applications will commence from 26 May 2026 and will continue until the post is filled.  For enquiries, please call Mr. TT Ho on (852) 2971 2700. The College reserves the right to fill or not to fill the post.  Applicants who are not contacted by the College 6 months after the application deadline may consider their applications unsuccessful. Application Deadline: Until the position(s) is/are filled All information and personal data collected will be used solely for recruitment related purposes.  For more information about the College, please visit our website: https://www.twc.edu.hk . WE ARE AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITIES EMPLOYER Apply now » Find similar jobs: Corporate Website Copyright & Disclaimer Privacy Policy ©2025 Tung Wah College Limited. All Rights Reserved"
    },
    "https://careers.twc.edu.hk/job/Senior-Lecturer-Senior-Clinical-Associate-in-Medical-Imaging-1392/1369575266/": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer / Senior Clinical Associate in Medical Imaging",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer / Senior Clinical Associate in Medical Imaging Job Details | TWC Skip to main content Search by Keyword Language English (United Kingdom) View profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Category All Unit / School All Apply now » Senior Lecturer / Senior Clinical Associate in Medical Imaging Tung Wah College Established by Tung Wah Group of Hospitals (“TWGHs”) in 2010, Tung Wah College (TWC) is a self-financing degree-granting institution registered under the Post Secondary Colleges Ordinance (Cap.320). Following the educational ideals of TWGHs and leveraging on its renowned strengths and expertise, TWC aims to provide high quality tertiary education to nurture competent, socially responsible and caring professionals for the benefits of society. With the staunch support of TWGHs, TWC has been developing rapidly and built up a niche in healthcare education. It is the first self-financing tertiary institution offering six professionally accredited degrees to train nurses and allied health professionals such as medical laboratory technologists, occupational therapists, diagnostic radiographer, therapeutic radiographer and physiotherapists. Besides, the College is also the first institution registered under Cap. 320 offering early childhood education degree and higher diploma programmes to train qualified kindergarten teachers and childcare professionals. Currently, TWC has 4 schools (namely School of Arts and Humanities, School of Management, School of Medical and Health Sciences, and School of Nursing) running a total of 20 doctoral degree, bachelor degree, sub-degree, diploma and certificate programmes in various disciplines.  It has a student population of around 5,000 in 2025/2026 and nurtured more than 7,200 graduates since its inception in 2010. Being a young and vibrant institution, TWC aspires to become a leading private university in the long term.  It is planning to launch a number of new programmes, strengthen teaching and learning facilities and quality, and enhance research capability etc. in coming years.  To cope with its continuous development, we are now inviting highly qualified candidates to fill the following post: Duties and Responsibilities For the position of Senior Lecturer (Full time / Fractional), the appointee will support: all aspects of academic activities, research, and consultancy; contribute to the planning, formulation and implementation of the College and School's strategic direction and development; participate in programme development and validation exercises; contribute to academic and school administration; take up responsibilities in academic and programme administration and clinical teaching; facilitate the College in enhancing its visibility and strengthening its local and international connections; build and develop an extensive network of contacts and colleagues to develop and enhance College market position and reputation; perform scholarly activities; facilitate the development and enhancement of the programme through quality research and publications including seeking external grants; oversee and perform academic activities including academic advising, examination and assessment, student recruitment, committee works, whole person development activities of students; and undertake professional service to external professional body / organization and provide public services to the community. For the position of Senior Clinical Associate (Full time / Fractional), the appointee will be required but not limited to: support teaching and learning activities, including preparing and developing teaching materials, delivering tutorials, classroom and laboratory-based practical classes; supervise students in their clinical projects and evaluate students’ clinical performance and skills in medical imaging, academic advising, provide support to co-curricular activities; coordinate student clinical placement with local, national and overseas healthcare agencies; contribute to the implementation of the strategic initiatives of the College and School; participate in programme development and validation exercises (focusing in clinical aspects); take up responsibilities in departmental administration; and undertake professional service to external professional body / organization and provide public services to the community. Qualifications and Experience Required For Senior Lecturer position (Full time / Fractional) , applicants should possess a Master’s degree in relevant discipline(Medical Imaging background is preferred) with sufficient years of post-registration clinical experience in a hospital setting; a valid Registered Radiographer practicing certificate issued by the Radiographers Board of Hong Kong with some research and teaching experience. For Senior Clinical Associate position (Full time / Fractional), applicants should possess a Master’s degree in relevant discipline (Medical Imaging background is preferred) with sufficient years of post-registration clinical experience in a hospital/clinic setting; a valid Registered Radiographer practicing certificate issued by the Radiographers Board of Hong Kong; demonstrate competence in clinical teaching and supervision with good communication skills. Application Salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. To apply, please submit your application via system.  The College reserves the right to fill or not to fill the post.  Applicants who are not contacted by the College 6 months after the application deadline may consider their applications unsuccessful. For enquiries, please phone or send WhatsApp to 9172-8618. Application Deadline: Until the positions are filled All information and personal data collected will be used solely for recruitment related purposes. For more information about the College, please visit our website: https://www.twc.edu.hk . Tung Wah College is an equal opportunities employer. We embrace the values of equality, diversity and inclusion and are dedicated to fostering an environment that respects and supports people with diverse perspectives, abilities, cultures and experiences. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Corporate Website Copyright & Disclaimer Privacy Policy ©2025 Tung Wah College Limited. All Rights Reserved"
    }
